WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.500
This is CyberScan. It lets you see inside any file before you open it.

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.500
Here's a file called invoice_2026.pdf.exe. It looks like a document.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Most security tools give you a red or a green light, and ask you to trust them.

4
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:21.000
CyberScan reads every byte, but it never runs a single one.

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
It lays the file out as cells, and measures how random each part is.

6
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Then nine engines examine it: the real file type, warning signs, YARA rules, program anatomy,

7
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.000
archive contents, signatures, a learning model, and optional threat intelligence.

8
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:43.000
Every signal is weighed into one score, never lower than the strongest evidence.

9
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.000
You get a verdict in plain words, in English or Arabic, with every finding explained.

10
00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:53.000
If something doesn't belong, CyberScan cuts it out of a copy. The original is kept.

11
00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:58.000
The removed parts are sealed in an encrypted vault, and the copy is checked.

12
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.500
Everything runs on your computer. Nothing is uploaded by default.

13
00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.000
And when it isn't sure, it tells you so.

14
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:13.500
Drop a file to begin. CyberScan.
